# Crisis Core –Final Fantasy VII– Reunion (PPSA07809, Unreal Engine 4.27 + IoStore)
# Reach the title screen: dismiss the autosave notice, then hold still.
#
# The boot sequence is: black -> white splash (several seconds) -> an "This game uses an autosave
# feature. / OK" dialog, which holds indefinitely -> the "Press Any Button" title screen with the
# version string and the Square Enix copyright. One Cross dismisses the dialog; nothing further is
# needed, and the title screen then holds for as long as the run lasts (verified to t=75 s).
#
# Anchored on DISPLAY FLIPS, not seconds: the pre-dialog load is IoStore-bound and its wall-clock
# length varies by tens of seconds between arms, while the flip at which the dialog appears is
# stable. Flip 120 is comfortably after it appears (~flip 100) and well before anything else.
#
# THIS ROUTE DOES NOT BOOT THE TITLE ON ITS OWN. A default run dies 5-12 s in, inside the guest's
# MallocBinned3 bundle-list pop (#1945), long before the dialog. The route was captured with the
# guest's submit call throttled, which is what gets past that fault:
#
#   PROSPER_GUEST_ARGS= PROSPER_NULL_PAGE=1 PROSPER_RENDER=1 PROSPER_MB3_POISON=1 \
#     PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT=@prosper/scripts/crisis-core/reach-title.pad \
#     ./build-linux/screenshot <DUMP_ROOT>/PPSA07809-app0 --seconds 1 --count 90 --timeout 180
#
# PROSPER_MB3_POISON is a read-only diagnostic, and using it as a throttle is a stopgap, not a fix
# — see docs/CRISIS_CORE_STATUS.md for the measurement that shows it is the DURATION of the scan
# and nothing it reads (PROSPER_SUBMIT_STALL_US=3000 substitutes for it; 500 us does not).
#
# STATUS: EXPLORATORY. Verified only as far as the title screen. Cross presses beyond that point
# open the new-game settings flow (voice language, then "Begin game with selected settings?"), so
# do not add blind presses here without re-capturing what they land on. Tracker: #1894.
f120-140:cross
